  "notes": "USAGE:\n{発覚|はっかく}する is almost exclusively used for negative things being exposed — crimes, scandals, lies, cheating, etc. For neutral or positive discoveries, {判明|はんめい}する or {明|あき}らかになる is used instead.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {不正|ふせい}が{発覚|はっかく}する (fraud is discovered)\n- {犯行|はんこう}が{発覚|はっかく}する (a crime is detected)\n- {嘘|うそ}が{発覚|はっかく}する (a lie is exposed)\n- {事件|じけん}が{発覚|はっかく}する (an incident comes to light)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {判明|はんめい}する: to become clear (neutral)\n- {露見|ろけん}する: to be exposed\n- {明|あき}るみに{出|で}る: to come to light",
